  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best is config_033 (scVI + ResNet50 + multiprofile + transformer + weighted) at 0.713 acc. The image modality is very weak alone (ResNet50 single: 0.208) yet adds ~6 points in the multimodal setting, suggesting it carries complementary signal. Key uncertainty: is the image encoder quality (ResNet50) the bottleneck limiting how much the image contributes, or is the signal inherently limited? Question: config_039 is identical to config_033 except the image encoder is swapped from ResNet50 to ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L, isolating the effect of image representation quality. Why best next: It is a clean single-variable extension of the best-performing configuration, directly testing whether a stronger image encoder unlocks more multimodal gain. If ViT-L substantially improves over ResNet50, it confirms the image modality has untapped signal and justifies further image-encoder investment; if not, it tells us the image contribution is near its ceiling and effort should shift to RNA-side improvements or fusion strategy. This is more informative than testing aggregation (avgpool vs transformer showed negligible difference in RNA-only) or fusion (weighted already beats concat by ~2.5 pts)."
}

